  <h1>After Cue’s launch day: <span class="accent">Cue, DSH, Grok Bot, Muse — a chooser for DSH readers</span></h1>
  <p class="muted small" style="margin-bottom:20px">September 29, 2026 · dshbase · X pulse</p>

  <p>Within hours of Cue’s September 28 launch, X stopped asking what Cue is and started asking which existing name it replaces. <a href="https://x.com/FacundoMarino1/status/2104726570116218890" rel="noopener noreferrer">@FacundoMarino1</a> put Cue next to Muse and Grok Bot in one question. <a href="https://x.com/wisereborn/status/2104735597193752773" rel="noopener noreferrer">@wisereborn</a> teased a guide. <a href="https://x.com/jhdxhl/status/2104717514584596757" rel="noopener noreferrer">@jhdxhl</a> reacted in Chinese. <a href="https://x.com/wjessup/status/2104709149112369436" rel="noopener noreferrer">@wjessup</a> was skeptical. That cluster is a mood, not a matrix. This pulse strips it down to lanes, for readers who already live in DeepSeek Harness and do not need a fourth product pitch. Cue and DSH are not 1:1 substitutes. Grok Bot and Muse are not DSH either. The useful act on launch day is to name the lane, then ignore the rest of the thread.</p>

  <h2>What the posts actually did</h2>
  <p>The maker’s posts are narrow. <a href="https://x.com/CueAgents/status/2104589146153181192" rel="noopener noreferrer">@CueAgents</a> said hello: personal agents, on Cue, at <a href="https://cue.im/" rel="noopener noreferrer">cue.im</a>. <a href="https://x.com/CueAgents/status/2104632868282769772" rel="noopener noreferrer">@CueAgents</a> said early access is free and limited, and named Android, Mac, and Windows. <a href="https://x.com/ManusAI/status/2104593894700990910" rel="noopener noreferrer">@ManusAI</a> introduced personal agents on Cue. The official description remains section 3 of the <a href="https://manus.im/blog/introducing-manus-2-0" rel="noopener noreferrer">Manus 2.0 post</a>: a standalone app, each agent with email, phone, wallet, and computer, group chat for handoff, you keep the final call. iOS is in App Store review. Phone numbers are in select countries, some voice-only. The starter invite mentioned in public is <strong>MEETCUE</strong>, and it is limited. A price after early access has not been published.</p>
  <p>The community posts did a different job. They grabbed the nearest consumer-agent names and asked for a winner. That is normal. It is also how a life-ops app, a desktop companion, a Meta Muse-lane product, and an open coding harness end up in one screenshot. @wjessup’s skepticism is a useful brake on that screenshot: a launch thread is not a field test. @jhdxhl is evidence the same compression happened in Chinese. @wisereborn is evidence people already want a buying guide. This note is a lane card, not that guide’s feature table. We do not have, and will not invent, a spec sheet for Grok Bot or Muse in order to fill a column.</p>

  <h2>A chooser, by lane</h2>
